description:
Replace the merged `scannedFiles` list with a structured per-layer outcome ledger for every expected evidence path.

`scanRepoByManifestLayers` currently unions orchestrator and personal-data file lists. This contaminates eligibility: a file processed by one layer can improperly enlarge another layer denominator, normally creating false negatives. Data-item any-match reuse can separately turn that contamination into false credit; one-to-one assignment fixes that different defect.

The ledger implements the complete reason model ruled on KDATAP-1b2294 and is emitted directly by ingest/layer processing rather than reconstructed from warning strings. It records the exact stage, normalized path, and reason.

For repository-level entities with multiple evidence locations:

- eligible when at least one supporting location was successfully processed for that layer;
- report full, partial, or no evidence coverage;
- entity denominators count the entity once;
- location/file coverage remains separately visible.

Related defect: personal-data-only scans currently take `scannedFiles` from whichever payload happens to be first. The new inventory and ledger remove that order dependence.

Definition of done: eligibility cannot be conferred across layers, all reason outcomes have contract tests, and materialized runs prove which packets actually encounter capacity limits.
